| 4h | RIGHT AFTER (ruled 2026-11-18) | genesis as floors (#/rulings, 2026-11-18: D1, D2, its three additions, the moʻolelo, the Nexus default; <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w26-floor-lane`>>): contact reads on the real house; one boot line naming the pinned floor beside the offered seed field by field, and the seed witness pinned for every seed source; the protect report and `/bulb` reading the stored island; the shadow read at mount; a floor format whose fields resolve to bytes (every floor CID moves, one genesis re-bake, Lares-Alpha baking); the flip once the operator's own house reads clean; adopt per ratchet as a `LocalFloor` beside the `ReleaseFloor`, its undo a forward revert, a release accept reading descent from the local floor's base; the whole-document merge (`reconcileGenesisCid`) retiring, its two-bakes reds (PR #225) carried into the adopt's tests; oracle to floor. BUILT (2026-11-18/19): both truths named, the boot, `floor status`, the kūkulu and `pulama admit` naming the founding record beside the offered seed (PR #230), and `lares vessel floor seed` reading the seed an image offers, which `up` hands the pūlama (PR #254, #261, #271); the protect report and `/bulb` reading the founding record (PR #227); the shadow read at each mount, off the boot path (PR #228); the floor format `{format, engine, plugins, snapshots}`, grammar leaving the manifest and `plugins` naming a signed offering, with Lares-Alpha's labelled re-bake (PR #256); the shadow tally counting per floor, and `reconcileGenesisCid` retired with its canon (PR #299, #302). A NAMED BRIDGE (PR #308, ruled 2026-11-19, road A of #/rulings): a founding floor of the prior shape mounts its snapshots alone, verified against its own canonical bytes, while pins, accepts, releases and cuts refuse it; it burns at a re-found or the local adopt, and until then the house's floor reads `predates` and counts no clean boot. Owed: contact reads on the real house (Wave 0, unread here); the flip (3c), once the operator's own house counts clean on a current floor; grammar beyond the floor (3b′) and oracle to floor (3f) on the next labelled re-bake. HELD: adopt per ratchet (3d), by the operator (backlog-awakens #/waves). Holder: Lares-Awakens (backlog-awakens Waves 0 to 3; plan lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/research/plan-floor-flip) | A standing house's island acts as a second registry beside its floor pin, and the floor manifest's fields go unread; the ruled shape moves only the pin. |

